# Figures and the embedded HTML are the report outputs no test reads, so they
# do not belong in git. The HTML in particular: with embed-resources it is a
# single file carrying every figure inline as base64, which git would store in
# full on every data refresh and no reviewer could read a diff of. Track them
# with DVC, or regenerate them from the pipeline, rather than committing them.
#
# The gfm output (report.md) is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the format the
# tests parse and the review diff reads, so it stays in git.
/figures
/report.html

/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
